    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches core P2P transaction download and orphanage logic across net_processing, TxOrphanage, and TxRequestTracker, accompanied by unit, fuzz, and functional tests.",
  "changed_since_previous": "The dedicated end-to-end fuzz harness (`p2p_1p1c_liveness`) was deferred out of this PR, and the dependency on #36437 was dropped.",
  "card": "This PR fixes four distinct liveness bugs in 1-parent-1-child (1p1c) package relay and orphan handling that allow peers to stall CPFP fee bumps. Previously, peer disconnections could permanently stall orphan reconsideration, reject filters could be poisoned by known transactions or witnessless copies, malleated parent announcements could purge valid child orphans across all peers, and witnessless parent rejections canceled pending txid orphan-parent requests. The patch ensures orphan handover on disconnect, prevents known transactions from entering reject filters, preserves orphans across package feerate failures, and adds typed announcement tracking in TxRequestTracker.",
